{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-68959",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "First, we rewrite the numerator using the power of product rule:\n\n$$\n\\frac{(5\\cdot 2)^{4}}{{5}^{3}}=\\frac{{5}^{4}\\cdot {2}^{4}}{{5}^{3}}=\n$$\n\nNext, we rewrite the fractional part of our expression as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{5}^{4}\\cdot {2}^{4}}{{5}^{3}} & =\\frac{{5}^{4}}{{5}^{3}}\\cdot {2}^{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rewrite the first fraction using the quotient rule for exponents, and then we simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{5}^{4}}{{5}^{3}}\\cdot {2}^{4} & ={5}^{4-3}\\cdot {2}^{4} \\\\  & ={5}^{1}\\cdot {2}^{4} \\\\  & =5\\cdot {2}^{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
